; Files.deleteIfExists(Path) returns false when the file did not exist. The
; false status is not an I/O exception; I/O failures are thrown separately.
; Go's native error result and Rust's core/std Result are the native arms:
; only exact declaration signatures prove them, and explicit blank
; assignments remain intentional discards.
(policy
  :schema-version 1
  :id "bifrost.correctness.ignored-status-result"
  :name "Ignored fallible result"
  :message "a fallible result is discarded"
  :severity note
  :description "The exact JDK 21 Files.deleteIfExists(Path) call returns a Boolean status: false means no file was deleted because it did not exist. Go calls whose resolved declaration has a native predeclared error result and Rust calls whose resolved declaration returns core/std Result are covered by the same result-use relation. An expression statement or for-loop initializer/update discards a result; an explicit blank assignment is intentional. Missing or conflicting contracts, shadowed Go error names, unproved Rust aliases, and unresolved dispatch remain incomplete. I/O exceptions and standard-library Write methods documented to never return an error remain separate. This diagnostic does not claim that every discarded fallible result is always a bug."
  :help-uri "https://bifrost.brokk.ai/static-analysis-policies/#built-in-code-smell-pack"
  :tags ["correctness" "java" "go" "rust" "result-use" "status"]
  :analysis (analysis
    :type assertion
    (bind :name discarded
      :query (rql :schema-version 1
        (union
          (filter :where ((obligation_kind eq fallible_status)
                          (failure_predicate eq (enum false))
                          (provenance eq reviewed)
                          (result_use eq discarded)
                          (coverage eq exhaustive)
                          (terminal eq false))
            (language java
              (call-result-obligations
                (call-shape (call :callee "deleteIfExists")))))
          (filter :where ((obligation_kind eq fallible_status)
                          (provenance eq native)
                          (result_use eq discarded)
                          (coverage eq exhaustive)
                          (terminal eq false))
            (language go
              (call-result-obligations
                (call-shape (call)))))
          (filter :where ((obligation_kind eq fallible_status)
                          (provenance eq native)
                          (result_use eq discarded)
                          (coverage eq exhaustive)
                          (terminal eq false))
            (language rust
              (call-result-obligations
                (call-shape (call))))))))
    (group :name by-call :by (discarded.id)
      (aggregate :name ignored-statuses :op count))
    (assert :group by-call :value ignored-statuses :cardinality (exactly 0))))
